# Generated and cached files that must never reach a commit.
#
# Nothing in here is a build input. build_site.py reads data/scores/ only,
# so ignoring the raw caches below cannot change what the site renders.

# Per-city caches of raw upstream responses — the street-level JSON that
# fetch_uk_city.py and fetch_london.py pull from data.police.uk. ~250 MB
# across 21 cities, rewritten on demand, and read only by the score_*.py
# step that turns them into the committed data/scores/ and
# data/counts_*.json. Committing them is what cost ~17 MB of permanent
# repo growth per city, which is unrecoverable once pushed.
data/raw/
data/raw_*/

# Two exceptions, committed on purpose: Berlin and Zurich are one-shot
# statistical downloads rather than a queryable rolling API, so there is no
# re-fetch to fall back on. Zurich's upstream CSV has been 404ing since
# 2 September 2026 (the breakage is on Kanton Zurich's publishing side) and
# fetch_zurich.py now exits 0 on failure specifically so the committed copy
# keeps serving the site's Zurich figures. These negations also keep
# `git add` from silently skipping a newly fetched
# data/raw_zurich/kreis_*.json.
!data/raw_berlin/
!data/raw_zurich/

# QA and reproducibility reports. qa_full_site.py and
# verify_reproducible.py default --report-dir to the repo root, and both CI
# workflows pass a relative "qa_output" from the root, which lands in the
# same place. pipeline/qa_output/ only appears if someone points
# --report-dir there by hand.
/qa_output/
pipeline/qa_output/

# The scratch build tree release.yml and reproducibility-check.yml create:
# a full copy of pipeline/ + data/ plus a freshly built dist/.
/candidate/

# Local cruft. dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored — Vercel serves the
# committed dist/, so the release commit has to contain it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
